Linux backend fallback: initialize Enigo (paste input synthesis) and
shortcuts even when the webview never loads. The frontend normally
calls initialize_enigo + initialize_shortcuts after the UI boots, but
the box-built AppImage's bundled WebKit EGL-aborts on the Fedora host,
so neither call came: ctrl+space stayed dead and ExternalScript paste
failed with 'Enigo state not initialized' (2026-07-17). Both commands
are idempotent, so backend + frontend both calling them is safe.
Applies on top of patches 01-04.

--- a/src-tauri/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src-tauri/src/lib.rs
@@ -571,6 +571,26 @@
                 show_main_window(&app_handle);
             }
 
+            // Linux: the frontend calls initialize_enigo + initialize_shortcuts
+            // once the webview loads, but a broken webview (e.g. bundled WebKit
+            // EGL-aborting on the host) must not leave dictation dead. Both
+            // commands are idempotent, so this backend fallback is safe
+            // alongside the frontend path. (The frontend-driven ordering only
+            // exists for macOS permission dialogs.)
+            #[cfg(target_os = "linux")]
+            {
+                let handle = app_handle.clone();
+                std::thread::spawn(move || {
+                    std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_secs(3));
+                    if let Err(e) = crate::commands::initialize_enigo(handle.clone()) {
+                        log::error!("Backend fallback enigo init failed: {}", e);
+                    }
+                    if let Err(e) = crate::commands::initialize_shortcuts(handle) {
+                        log::error!("Backend fallback shortcut init failed: {}", e);
+                    }
+                });
+            }
+
             Ok(())
         })
         .on_window_event(|window, event| match event {
